<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- W3C SCXML 3.7: only a <final> whose parent is the <scxml> element ends
     the session.

     Appendix D `enterStates` splits the two cases in one branch:

       if isFinalState(s):
           if isSCXMLElement(s.parent):
               running = false
           else:
               parent = s.parent
               internalQueue.enqueue(new Event("done.state." + parent.id, s.donedata))

     So `isFinalState(s)` — "s is a <final> element" — is a structural
     question, and it is not by itself the machine-completion criterion. An
     engine that answers "has this session ended?" with the bare structural
     predicate reports completion the moment a compound state finishes, while
     the machine is still live and still able to take transitions.

     (Appendix D's separate `isInFinalState(s)` helper is a third thing again
     — it asks whether a compound or parallel state has completed, for the
     done.state computation. The name similarity is the whole trap.)

     The machine has to *rest* in the nested final for the difference to be
     observable: if something carries it onward inside the same macrostep,
     both a right and a wrong completion predicate are only ever sampled at
     the end. So nothing here consumes `done.state.phase` — `phase` is
     finished and the machine simply waits, exactly as a compound state that
     has completed its work and awaits its next external stimulus.

       ends only on a top-level final   not complete after initialize;
                                        `resume` still reaches `pass`
       ends on any final                reports complete while resting in
                                        phaseDone, with pass unreachable

     Deliberately single-axis: no `<invoke>`, no autoforward, no `<parallel>`,
     no delay. A regional `<final>` inside a `<parallel>` reaches the same
     Appendix D branch, but mixing the two would let a parallel-completion
     regression masquerade as this one.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       version="1.0" datamodel="ecmascript" initial="phase"
       name="nested_final_not_terminal">
    <state id="phase" initial="running">
        <state id="running">
            <transition target="phaseDone"/>
        </state>
        <final id="phaseDone"/>
        <transition event="resume" target="pass"/>
    </state>
    <final id="pass"/>
</scxml>
